From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] modules: use AM_LDFLAGS instead of blanking LDFLAGS

src/modules/Makefile.am assigns to LDFLAGS directly:

    LDFLAGS =
    if DARWIN_HOST
    LDFLAGS += -Wl,-U,_module_speak -Wl,-U,_module_speak_sync
    endif

LDFLAGS is a user variable. Clearing it discards whatever the build environment
passed in for everything under src/modules/, while the rest of the tree (for
instance src/api/c) keeps it. Under OpenEmbedded that silently drops
-Wl,-O1 -Wl,--hash-style=gnu -Wl,--as-needed, so libspeechd_module.so is linked
without a GNU hash section and package QA rejects it:

  QA Issue: File /usr/lib/libspeechd_module.so.0.0.0 in package speech-dispatcher
  doesn't have GNU_HASH (didn't pass LDFLAGS?)

AM_LDFLAGS is the maintainer-facing variable meant for this, and automake emits
both it and $(LDFLAGS) in its link rules, so the Darwin workaround keeps working
while the environment's flags survive. Per-target settings such as
sd_ibmtts_LDFLAGS are unaffected: those replace AM_LDFLAGS but automake still
appends $(LDFLAGS) after them.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/modules/Makefile.am | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/Makefile.am b/src/modules/Makefile.am
index 8f8c09d..166adfe 100644
--- a/src/modules/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/modules/Makefile.am
@@ -27,10 +27,10 @@ EXTRA_DIST += dummy-message.txt
 CLEANFILES = dummy-message.wav
 
 inc_local = -I$(top_srcdir)/include -I$(top_srcdir)/src/common
-LDFLAGS =
+AM_LDFLAGS =
 
 if DARWIN_HOST
-LDFLAGS += -Wl,-U,_module_speak -Wl,-U,_module_speak_sync
+AM_LDFLAGS += -Wl,-U,_module_speak -Wl,-U,_module_speak_sync
 endif
 
 AM_CFLAGS = $(ERROR_CFLAGS)
-- 
